Z||000001||TopFiero||08-31-2001||12:31 PM||||  In my old racing years, I frequently pitted my 1985 SE V-6 4-speed and 1987 SE V-6 5-speed against a variety of MR2's at official drag strips (with time cards).  Both Fieros were near stock, only slight intake and exhaust improvements.  The 1985-1989 years were easy to defeat, naturally aspirated.  I also never lost to a Supercharged edition, 15.5 @ 89 vs. 15.6 @ 87 were the normal times.  The 1991+ NA version seemed more of a dog then the '85-'89, but the Turbo model was a force to be reckoned with.  My friend had an '89 SC so we enjoyed friendly stoplight drags all the time.  Lots of fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tonker||08-31-2001||01:25 PM||||No way a normally aspirated Mk1 can take a v6 Fiero. I've raced two of them and they've both lost. I don't know about he SC since I've never even seen one. My guess is the SC might give it the extra power it needs to keep up with the v6. The turbo mk2s are awesome though.||||reg||1
