Z||000008||TopFiero||08-31-2001||05:22 PM||||  Does anyone remember the little competition I offered in 1995 from my website?  Probably not too many of you.  I offered to sponsor a friendly drag race at a strip (Firebird Raceway), this was a neutral location that everyone could meet at.  I challenged all MR2 owners to show up and I would front the money for everybody's racing fees (around $8 per car that day).  We had a number of Fieros show up and only 3 MR2's, lol.  Perhaps the MR2 crowd needs a reminder.  Keep it nice and friendly... offer to arrange a drag race day and let everyone show up that's willing to make the drive.  Post the time cards on the internet when it's over.  It will probably resolve the issue very nicely.  Also realize that MR2 and Fiero owners have a lot more in common than many of them are willing to admit.  We should join ranks for the enthusiasm we all share for mid-engine sports cars.  Also remind these MR2 fans that nearly 50% of all V-6 Fieros have automatic transmissions, meaning they are substantially slower then the manual version, usually right between the manual V-6 and the 2.5 4-cylinder.  In testing, times we got for 0-60 were about 7.5 for the stick, 8.7-9.5 for the automatic, and 10.8-11.5 for the 4-cylinder.||||reg||1
